.Dd November 27, 2026
.Dt USBCONSOLED 8
.Os NextBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm usbconsoled
.Nd give the console user the USB devices no kernel driver claims
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Scanners, cameras and other devices driven from user space with
.Xr libusb 3
have no kernel driver; programs open their
.Xr ugen 4
nodes,
.Pa /dev/usb/ Ns Ar bus . Ns Ar address . Ns Ar endpoint ,
which
.Xr devfs 4
creates owned by root, mode 0600.
.Nm
gives those nodes to the person logged in at the console, mode 0660, so
that their programs (Scanner, SANE's
.Xr scanimage 1 )
can use the device, and gives them back to root when they log out.
.Pp
A device qualifies if it is not a hub and at least one interface of its
configuration has no kernel driver attached.
Interfaces a driver has stay the kernel's.
The console user is configd's
.Li State:/Users/ConsoleUser ,
which
.Xr consoleuser 8
publishes at login, as
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8
uses it for removable disks.
.Pp
NextBSD runs no
.Xr devd 8 ,
so
.Nm
reads
.Pa /dev/usb
every two seconds; a device that appears is looked at once.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl n
Change nothing; log what would be done.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nextbsd.usbconsoled.plist
.It Pa /var/log/usbconsoled.log
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr consoleuser 8 ,
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8 ,
.Xr ugen 4 ,
.Xr usbconfig 8
